c","description":"The th in \'think\'","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-54f8-77ef-b193-cc61b1e6853a","description":"The ch in \'cheese\'","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-54f8-72fa-90fe-cf7fbafdaaf3","description":"The j in \'juice\'","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-54f8-73a8-a22d-b74bb2ff5ced","description":"The t in \'train\'","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-54f8-76c9-a132-81b1630e989d","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7095-8a30-44480fe2c4f5","question":"What is the meaning of the name of the constellation Cygnus?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Cygnus is Latin for swan. Its bright stars also form the Northern Cross, a prominent asterism.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-54f8-72ae-aaf2-2299108f4474","description":"Swan","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-54f8-7427-b35d-68bb07a08b68","description":"Ring","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-54f8-7df1-9773-f3f7d04359e5","description":"River","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-54f8-7221-886b-98026b9a34d2","description":"Mountain","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-54f8-7cc8-938b-666e1edc00d7","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7095-8a30-44480fe2c4f5","question":"Although the Poodle is widely associated with France, in which country is it believed to have originated?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"The Poodle\u2019s name is linked to the word \u201cPudel,\u201d referring to splashing in water; the breed was developed as a water retriever.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-54f8-78f4-b57d-2eb1796a8c2b","description":"Germany","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-54f8-778b-a638-b345291aa92e","description":"Egypt","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-54f8-7f8a-869f-8d0021fd6f5b","description":"India","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-54f8-7530-b8f2-71086880b859","description":"Spain","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-54f8-7f4a-a132-cc188f5aaead","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7095-8a30-44480fe2c4f5","question":"What was built by CERN near Geneva?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"CERN\u2019s Large Hadron Collider lies beneath the French-Swiss border and lets scientists study matter through high-energy collisions.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-54f8-77f6-8b89-ab67f4c455ae","description":"Particle accelerator","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-54f8-7b62-a847-dc0b18fb522f","description":"Art museum","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-54f8-7e4f-984c-20807e8a7d70","description":"Colossus computer","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-54f8-7816-a972-809091ac4e5b","description":"Rocket launch pad","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-54f8-7acc-912d-65338f323135","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7095-8a30-44480fe2c4f5","question":"What was Rubik\'s Cube originally called when Ern\u0151 Rubik invented it in 1974?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"The Magic Cube was developed as a teaching tool for three-dimensional geometry before it was marketed internationally under Rubik\u2019s name.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-54f8-7fc5-99ef-8e1983d289d6","description":"Magic Cube","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-54f8-7e10-852f-f6da85ed7dcd","description":"Wonder Cube","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-54f8-7183-b55e-e26decc0f521","description":"Hungarian Box","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-54f8-746c-9167-15ec65053f40","description":"Colour Block","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-54f8-70e7-bcf6-887a35889fed","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7095-8a30-44480fe2c4f5","question":"According to the biblical story of Cain and Abel, what type of animals did Abel offer as a sacrifice to God?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Genesis says Abel brought the firstborn of his flock as an offering, identifying the animals as sheep.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-54f8-7522-948a-dfe0a53720d5","description":"Sheep","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-54f8-759c-8994-2b3574176048","description":"Cows","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-54f8-7082-a85f-cb3